    "goal": "Report the per-chromosome .bed size, total binary .bed size, and number of per-chromosome files for a GWAS genotype dataset of 8424 samples and 7,598,278 variants.",
    "rationale": "The binary .bed format packs 2 bits per sample per variant, so total size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome size uses the same rule applied to the largest chromosome's variant count (231,808). The number of per-chromosome files equals the number of chromosomes in the dataset. With 7,598,278 total variants and 231,808 on the largest chromosome, this is a standard human GWAS; the per-chromosome file count is the number of chromosomes (22 autosomes + X + Y + MT = 25).",
